---
import LearnArticle from "../../components/LearnArticle.astro";
import DemoFrame from "../../components/DemoFrame.astro";

const worstCases = [
	{ size: "10", linear: "10", binary: "4" },
	{ size: "100", linear: "100", binary: "7" },
	{ size: "1,000", linear: "1,000", binary: "10" },
	{ size: "1 million", linear: "1 million", binary: "20" },
	{ size: "1 billion", linear: "1 billion", binary: "30" },
];

const lanes = [
	{ id: "linear", name: "Linear search", how: "Check 1, then 2, then 3…" },
	{ id: "binary", name: "Binary search", how: "Always guess the middle" },
];
---

<LearnArticle
	href="/learn/binary-search"
	description="Binary search explained with a hands-on demo: find a hidden number by halving the possibilities each guess, and compare it with a one-by-one linear search."
	lead="You've been doing this the whole time. Every LogicDash guess uses feedback to make the next guess smarter — binary search is the most famous version of that idea."
>
	<section class="block">
		<p class="block-title">The Guessing Game</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			"I'm thinking of a number from 1 to 100. After each guess, I'll tell you if the answer is
			higher or lower."
		</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			You could guess 1, then 2, then 3, and so on. You'd get there eventually — but it might take
			100 guesses. Almost nobody plays that way. Instead, most people start with{" "}
			<span class="mono-highlight">50</span>. If the answer is "higher," every number from 1 to 50
			is gone in one guess. Then they try <span class="mono-highlight">75</span>, and so on.
		</p>
		<p class="block-callout">
			Binary search: guess the middle, throw away the half that can't be right, repeat.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<p class="block-title">Two Ways to Search</p>
		<div class="compare-grid">
			<div class="compare-card">
				<p class="compare-card-title">Linear search</p>
				<p>Check every item in order, one at a time, until you find it.</p>
				<p>Works on <em>any</em> list, even a jumbled one. Slow on long lists.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="compare-card compare-card--accent">
				<p class="compare-card-title">Binary search</p>
				<p>Check the middle item, then keep only the half that could hold the answer.</p>
				<p>Much faster — but <em>only works if the list is already sorted</em>.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<DemoFrame label="Binary search demo">
		<div class="bs-demo" data-bs-demo>
			<div class="demo-field">
				<label for="bs-range">Hidden number between 1 and</label>
				<select id="bs-range" class="demo-select" data-bs-range>
					<option value="100" selected>100</option>
					<option value="1000">1,000</option>
				</select>
			</div>
			<div class="demo-field">
				<label for="bs-pick">Choose the hidden number yourself (optional)</label>
				<input id="bs-pick" class="demo-input bs-pick" type="number" min="1" max="100" inputmode="numeric" data-bs-pick />
				<button type="button" class="demo-btn" data-bs-use-pick>Hide it</button>
			</div>

			<p class="bs-secret">
				Hidden number: <span class="bs-secret-value" data-bs-secret>?</span>
				<button type="button" class="bs-reveal" data-bs-reveal aria-pressed="false">Show</button>
			</p>

			<div class="bs-lanes">
				{
					lanes.map((lane) => (
						<div class="bs-lane" data-bs-lane={lane.id}>
							<p class="bs-lane-name">{lane.name}</p>
							<p class="bs-lane-how">{lane.how}</p>
							<div class="bs-track" aria-hidden="true">
								<div class="bs-track-remaining" data-bs-remaining />
								<div class="bs-track-marker" data-bs-marker hidden />
							</div>
							<div class="bs-track-ends" aria-hidden="true">
								<span>1</span>
								<span data-bs-max-label>100</span>
							</div>
							<p class="bs-lane-guess" data-bs-guess>No guesses yet</p>
							<div class="bs-lane-stats">
								<div class="demo-stat">
									<span class="demo-stat-value" data-bs-count>0</span>
									<span class="demo-stat-label">Guesses</span>
								</div>
								<div class="demo-stat">
									<span class="demo-stat-value" data-bs-left>100</span>
									<span class="demo-stat-label">Still possible</span>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</div>

			<div class="demo-controls">
				<button type="button" class="demo-btn demo-btn--primary" data-bs-step>Next guess</button>
				<button type="button" class="demo-btn" data-bs-run>Run to the end</button>
				<button type="button" class="demo-btn" data-bs-new>New hidden number</button>
			</div>
			<p class="demo-status" data-bs-status aria-live="polite">
				Press “Next guess” — both searches take one guess at a time.
			</p>
		</div>
	</DemoFrame>

	<section class="block block--example">
		<p class="block-title">Why Halving Is So Powerful</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			Each binary-search guess cuts the possibilities in half. Double the size of the list, and you
			only need <em>one</em> more guess. Here's the most guesses each method could ever need (the worst case):
		</p>
		<div class="table-wrap">
			<table class="data-table">
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th>Numbers to search</th>
						<th>Linear</th>
						<th>Binary</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					{
						worstCases.map((row) => (
							<tr>
								<td class="num">{row.size}</td>
								<td class="num">{row.linear}</td>
								<td class="num">{row.binary}</td>
							</tr>
						))
					}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p class="block-text">
			Notice the binary column: 7 guesses covers 100 numbers because 7 halvings is the same as the
			doubling you've seen with bits — 2<sup>7</sup> = 128, which is more than 100. Thirty guesses
			is enough to search a <em>billion</em> sorted items.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<p class="block-title">The Catch: It Has to Be Sorted</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			Binary search only works because "higher" or "lower" tells you which half to throw away. That
			only makes sense if the items are in order. You can't binary-search a shuffled deck of cards —
			the middle card tells you nothing about where the others are.
		</p>
		<p class="block-text">
			That's why computers spend so much effort sorting data: sorting once makes every later search
			fast. See how sorting works on the <a href="/learn/sorting-algorithms">Sorting Algorithms</a> page.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block">
		<p class="block-title">Where You'll Meet It</p>
		<ul class="block-list">
			<li>Looking up a word in a paper dictionary — you open near the middle, not at page one.</li>
			<li>Finding a contact in your phone, or a product in a huge online store.</li>
			<li>Programmers hunting for the exact change that broke their code, by testing halfway points.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</LearnArticle>

<script>
	type LaneId = "linear" | "binary";
	interface LaneState {
		lo: number;
		hi: number;
		count: number;
		lastGuess: number | null;
		found: boolean;
	}

	const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bs-demo]")!;
	const rangeSelect = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("[data-bs-range]")!;
	const pickInput = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-bs-pick]")!;
	const usePickBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-bs-use-pick]")!;
	const secretEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bs-secret]")!;
	const revealBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-bs-reveal]")!;
	const stepBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-bs-step]")!;
	const runBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-bs-run]")!;
	const newBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-bs-new]")!;
	const statusEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bs-status]")!;

	let max = 100;
	let secret = 1;
	let revealed = false;
	let runTimer: number | null = null;
	const lanes: Record<LaneId, LaneState> = {
		linear: freshLane(),
		binary: freshLane(),
	};

	function freshLane(): LaneState {
		return { lo: 1, hi: max, count: 0, lastGuess: null, found: false };
	}

	function laneEl(id: LaneId) {
		return root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-bs-lane="${id}"]`)!;
	}

	function reset(newSecret?: number) {
		stopRun();
		secret = newSecret ?? 1 + Math.floor(Math.random() * max);
		lanes.linear = freshLane();
		lanes.binary = freshLane();
		revealed = false;
		render();
		statusEl.textContent = "New hidden number chosen. Press “Next guess” to start.";
	}

	function nextGuess(id: LaneId, lane: LaneState): number {
		// Linear walks upward one by one; binary always takes the middle of
		// whatever range is still possible.
		return id === "linear" ? lane.lo : Math.floor((lane.lo + lane.hi) / 2);
	}

	function stepLane(id: LaneId): string | null {
		const lane = lanes[id];
		if (lane.found) return null;
		const guess = nextGuess(id, lane);
		lane.count += 1;
		lane.lastGuess = guess;
		if (guess === secret) {
			lane.found = true;
			lane.lo = lane.hi = guess;
			return `found it in ${lane.count} ${lane.count === 1 ? "guess" : "guesses"}`;
		}
		if (guess < secret) lane.lo = guess + 1;
		else lane.hi = guess - 1;
		return `guessed ${guess} — ${guess < secret ? "too low" : "too high"}`;
	}

	function step(announce: boolean) {
		const linearMsg = stepLane("linear");
		const binaryMsg = stepLane("binary");
		render();
		const done = lanes.linear.found && lanes.binary.found;
		if (done) {
			stopRun();
			statusEl.textContent = `Both found ${secret}. Linear search took ${lanes.linear.count} guesses; binary search took ${lanes.binary.count}.`;
		} else if (announce) {
			const parts = [];
			if (linearMsg) parts.push(`Linear ${linearMsg}.`);
			if (binaryMsg) parts.push(`Binary ${binaryMsg}.`);
			statusEl.textContent = parts.join(" ");
		}
	}

	function render() {
		secretEl.textContent = revealed || (lanes.linear.found && lanes.binary.found) ? String(secret) : "?";
		revealBtn.textContent = revealed ? "Hide" : "Show";
		revealBtn.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(revealed));

		(["linear", "binary"] as LaneId[]).forEach((id) => {
			const lane = lanes[id];
			const el = laneEl(id);
			const remaining = el.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bs-remaining]")!;
			const marker = el.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bs-marker]")!;
			const guessEl = el.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bs-guess]")!;
			const pct = (n: number) => ((n - 1) / Math.max(1, max - 1)) * 100;

			remaining.style.left = `${pct(lane.lo)}%`;
			remaining.style.width = `max(3px, ${pct(lane.hi) - pct(lane.lo)}%)`;
			marker.hidden = lane.lastGuess === null;
			if (lane.lastGuess !== null) marker.style.left = `${pct(lane.lastGuess)}%`;

			el.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bs-count]")!.textContent = String(lane.count);
			el.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bs-left]")!.textContent = String(lane.hi - lane.lo + 1);
			el.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-bs-max-label]")!.textContent = max.toLocaleString();
			el.classList.toggle("is-found", lane.found);

			if (lane.lastGuess === null) guessEl.textContent = "No guesses yet";
			else if (lane.found) guessEl.textContent = `✓ Found it: ${lane.lastGuess}`;
			else guessEl.textContent = `Guessed ${lane.lastGuess} — ${lane.lastGuess < secret ? "too low ↑" : "too high ↓"}`;
		});

		const done = lanes.linear.found && lanes.binary.found;
		stepBtn.disabled = done;
		runBtn.disabled = done && runTimer === null;
		runBtn.textContent = runTimer === null ? "Run to the end" : "Pause";
	}

	function stopRun() {
		if (runTimer !== null) {
			window.clearInterval(runTimer);
			runTimer = null;
		}
	}

	function toggleRun() {
		if (runTimer !== null) {
			stopRun();
			render();
			statusEl.textContent = "Paused.";
			return;
		}
		// Fast enough that linear search finishes in a few seconds even at
		// 1,000 — binary search will already be done long before that, which
		// is exactly the point.
		const interval = max > 100 ? 12 : 70;
		runTimer = window.setInterval(() => step(false), interval);
		render();
		statusEl.textContent = "Running…";
	}

	rangeSelect.addEventListener("change", () => {
		max = Number(rangeSelect.value);
		pickInput.max = String(max);
		reset();
	});

	usePickBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
		const value = Math.round(Number(pickInput.value));
		if (!Number.isFinite(value) || value < 1 || value > max) {
			statusEl.textContent = `Pick a whole number from 1 to ${max.toLocaleString()}.`;
			pickInput.focus();
			return;
		}
		pickInput.value = "";
		reset(value);
		statusEl.textContent = "Your number is hidden. Press “Next guess” to watch both searches hunt for it.";
	});

	pickInput.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
		if (event.key === "Enter") usePickBtn.click();
	});

	revealBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
		revealed = !revealed;
		render();
	});

	stepBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
		stopRun();
		step(true);
	});
	runBtn.addEventListener("click", toggleRun);
	newBtn.addEventListener("click", () => reset());

	reset();
</script>

<style is:global>
	.bs-demo .bs-pick {
		width: 6.5em;
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-secret {
		margin: 0.9em 0 0;
		text-align: center;
		font-size: 1em;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-secret-value {
		display: inline-block;
		min-width: 2.5em;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 1.3em;
		color: #fff3d6;
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-reveal {
		margin-left: 0.4em;
		padding: 0.25em 0.8em;
		min-height: 2.2em;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: transparent;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.85em;
		font-weight: 600;
		cursor: pointer;
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-reveal:hover,
	.bs-demo .bs-reveal:focus-visible {
		border-color: var(--color-accent);
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-lanes {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 16em), 1fr));
		gap: 0.8em;
		margin-top: 0.9em;
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-lane {
		padding: 0.85em 1em;
		border-radius: 12px;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		background: var(--color-bg);
		text-align: center;
		transition: border-color 0.2s ease;
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-lane.is-found {
		border-color: var(--color-accent);
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-lane-name {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 1.05em;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-lane-how {
		margin: 0.1em 0 0.7em;
		font-size: 0.9em;
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-track {
		position: relative;
		height: 1.1em;
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-border) 70%, transparent);
		overflow: hidden;
	}

	/* The shaded span is "numbers that could still be the answer" — it
	   shrinks as guesses rule numbers out. */
	.bs-demo .bs-track-remaining {
		position: absolute;
		top: 0;
		bottom: 0;
		background: linear-gradient(90deg, #ffae2e, #ffc766);
		border-radius: 999px;
		transition:
			left 0.25s ease,
			width 0.25s ease;
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-track-marker {
		position: absolute;
		top: -0.1em;
		bottom: -0.1em;
		width: 3px;
		margin-left: -1px;
		background: #fff;
		box-shadow: 0 0 4px #000;
		transition: left 0.25s ease;
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-track-ends {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		margin-top: 0.2em;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.8em;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-lane-guess {
		margin: 0.6em 0 0;
		min-height: 1.5em;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 0.95em;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-lane-stats {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: center;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.5em;
		margin-top: 0.6em;
	}

	.bs-demo .bs-lane-stats .demo-stat {
		min-width: 6.5em;
		background: var(--color-surface);
	}
</style>
